  "measured": "MEASURED BEFORE BUILDING (tools/cast_shadows/evidence/jamb/). (a) Not a flat quad: same code path as the pillar's face, each column one column of its own face; flat-lit (energy 0, ambient x8 \u2014 a measurement capture) the jamb's east face cv 0.35 against its own front's 0.34, the pillar's 0.53 against 0.36, run ends 0.30/0.18 \u2014 the family's per-tile range; hue r/b identical (0.99). (b) The hard edge was NOT a shadow edge: penumbrae beside the jamb 28-30 px, the pillar's 33-40 px (softness 12.0, all within one kernel). It was the EAST-FACE SPRITE'S OWN BOUNDARY: inheriting the first-surface mask exemption, the face sat at (59.7, r/b 2.89) with and without occluders while the corridor floor it hangs over went 141 -> 85 in the jamb's own shadow. FIX: the east face takes the ground mask (one bit, Tier1BoundaryWall.cs). AFTER, lamp-only: in the jamb's shadow the face reads (33,33,42) beside the shadowed floor's (40,41,53) \u2014 the same ambient-hued dark at its own albedo \u2014 and its hue flips with the shadow exactly as the floor's does (2.41 -> 0.80 vs 1.96 -> 0.82); at the regime the fire lights it from the east (r/b 1.19). The pillar's east face stays lit (factor 0.93; the lamp is on its side). BAR AS DECLARED, HELD FROZEN AND IMPEACHED (LOOP-PROCESS \u00a78): term 1 'cv within 0.10 of the pillar' NOT MET on the number (0.35 vs 0.53) \u2014 the reference was wrong, the family's own tiles vary 0.13-0.53 and each east face tracks its own front; term 2 'ratio step <= 0.10' NOT MET as written (0.37) \u2014 a with/without luminance ratio is not material-independent under a hue-replacing shadow colour, so the instrument, not the fix, was mis-specified; the honest measure is the lamp-only RGB above. Penumbra-width and pillar-lit terms MET. No \u00a76.2 value moved.",
